    "id": "overlap-pilot",
    "language": "Here we find ourselves in a mirrored position at the same drill as before. We're again in a two v one scenario, and we're trying to score. The attacking player with the ball will approach the defender. The defender will shut him down, leaving me the opportunity to go towards the goal. It is really important that th- our teammate gets the ball to us without making it too predictable for the teammate to prevent the ball from getting to me. This means that the, my teammate here needs to be quick and aware of how quick the defender is shutting him down. So here I will run into the space. And now that I am perfectly in the space in about a 45-degree angle, I will unpause, receive the ball, and now I've been shut down before I've received the ball, so I will have to pass back to my teammate, and he will score... since I am shut down by this defender.",
